      </figure>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Frontispiece</p>
      <h2 class="sec-title" style="margin:.4rem 0 1rem"><span class="mask"><span class="mask-in">Contents — An Index of the Bills</span></span></h2>
      <p class="lede">Hereafter shall appear, one after another, twenty-five limericks concerning persons of the name of Bill — bakers, butchers, <span style="border-bottom:1px dotted var(--madder)">economists</span>, boatmen, and one gentleman of the Rhineland who dined with a <span style="border-bottom:1px dotted var(--madder)">Jurgen</span>. Each plate is struck in type, footed in meter, and offered, as is the custom, without charge of conscience.</p>
      <ol class="index" id="indexList"></ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ NOTE ON FORM ============ -->
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="sec-orn"><i>❦</i></div>
    <h2 class="sec-title"><span class="mask"><span class="mask-in">A Note on the Form</span></span></h2>
  </section>
  <div class="form-grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The limerick is the humblest of poems: five lines, three rhymes, and a small but binding obligation to be funny. Its first and last lines are the long ones — the gallopers — while the middle pair are short, so that the verse may tuck its joke away and bring it back at the end, like a dog with a stick.</p>
      <p>Its engine is the anapest: two soft syllables chased by one hard one. Strike the specimen at the side, and you will hear the little trot that carries every Bill in this book.</p>
      <dl class="gloss">
        <div><dt>AABBA</dt><dd>The rhyme scheme: two long lines, two short, and one long line that lands the joke.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Anapest</dt><dd>A three-syllable foot, stressed on the last. The gallop of the verse; da-da-DUM.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Limerick</dt><dd>A town in Ireland which has, on record, never had to hear a single one of these.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="specimen">
      <p class="eyebrow">Specimen — the anapest, struck</p>
      <p class="spec-line" id="specLine"></p>
      <button class="btn" id="scanBtn">Strike the Meter</button>
      <p class="spec-legend">● = the hard syllable; the others are merely the chase.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ THE READING ============ -->
  <div class="reading">
    <aside class="rail" aria-label="Reading tools">
      <div class="rail-ink"><span>Ink Remaining</span><span id="inkPct">100%</span><div class="gauge"><i id="gaugeFill"></i></div></div>
      <div>
        <p class="rail-h">The Index</p>
        <nav class="rail-index" id="railIndex"></nav>
      </div>
